# Photograph the sneak-attack gate for a rogue's FIRST blow from Improved
# Invisibility, and the matching control in plain sight. Part of bead inc-nkf2.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-sneak-invis.dat \
#   INCURSION_SNEAK_PROBE=1 \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/sneak-invis-melee.keys <seed>
#
# Read the result with tools/check_sneak_invis.sh, which runs this script
# across many seeds and tallies the probe lines. This file only produces the
# session and its logs/sneak.log.
#
# THE SPELL. lib/wspells.irh:6618 "Improved Invisibility" grants INVIS at
# INV_NORMAL (1) and, per its own Desc, recurs 1d4+1 rounds after an attack
# breaks it. INV_NORMAL is not INV_IMPROVED, so src/Fight.cpp:4166-4169 strips
# the INVIS on the first blow. Only the first blow after each cast is from
# invisibility; only that blow is measured here.
#
# THE VICTIM. A brown bear (lib/mon1.irh:4085) is summoned because it is
# SZ_MEDIUM, has no M_SEE_INVIS and no FT_BLIND_FIGHT, and -- unlike the
# ettercap -- does not web the player or hide. It is animal-Intelligence, so
# its Listen rating is low, which gives the rogue's Move Silently a fair
# contest (src/Fight.cpp:4184-4191).
#
# WHY THE ROOM IS LIT. Perceives() (src/Vision.cpp) lets a monster see the
# player in an unlit room only through infravision, and invisibility skips
# even that (the INVIS test at :907 jumps over the infravision block at :947).
# In the dark the bear cannot see the player AT ALL, so even a plainly visible
# control blow would be "unseen" and would open the sneak gate by itself. A
# standing Call Light (lib/pspells.irh:167) onto the player's own square makes
# the tile lit, so the bear perceives the rogue normally while visible; only
# invisibility then denies it. The rogue is an orc, which is M_LIGHT_AVERSE, so
# it takes a -4 to hit in the light (src/Fight.cpp:4424) -- a cost, not a
# confound, and the check counts across enough seeds to land blows anyway.
#
# GETTING THE VICTIM NON-FLAT-FOOTED. A freshly summoned creature has a high
# FFCount (src/Monster.cpp:1457), so it is flat-footed (inc/Creature.h:643) and
# a visible blow on it would open the gate on its own. The setup blow below
# both walks into the bear (prompting "Confirm attack") and zeroes both
# fighters' FFCount (src/Fight.cpp:4147-4148), whether or not it lands. The
# control blow after it is therefore at a non-flat-footed victim.
#
# Freeze Monsters is deliberately NOT enabled: it makes every victim flat-
# footed (inc/Creature.h:227) and would spoil both measurements. Cheat Death is
# enabled so the bear cannot end the session mid-resolution (a death prompt
# before the sneak gate would swallow the probe line); "n" in the die prompt
# takes the engine's own "You cheat death" branch (src/Fight.cpp:8596).
#
# SEED. The attribute rolls, the offered feats and the Move Silently vs Listen
# rolls all move with the seed, so one seed is one trial.

@include sneak-invis-chargen.keys

SPACE   # dismiss the arrival-room description

# Wizard mode: Cheat Death (row 1) so a killing blow offers the prompt instead
# of ending the run, and Infinite Mana (row 8) because Improved Invisibility
# costs 40 mana and a 1st-level rogue has 19.
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
SPACE
DOWN*7
SPACE
ESC

# Teach the rogue both spells. Learn Any Spell sets SP_KNOWN|SP_PRIMAL|SP_INNATE
# (src/Debug.cpp:862), which is enough for SpellManager(SM_CAST) to offer them.
w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Call Light" ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC
w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Improved Invisibility" ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC

# Call Light, standing radiance, on our own square: a lit arena.
m
@cursorto:mark "Call Light" DOWN
ENTER
*
s
@while "Take opportunity" y
@while "Die?" n
@dump:lit

# Summon the victim one square east (SZ_MEDIUM, so the placement cursor's
# default tile holds it).
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Animals"
@choose "brown bear"
RIGHT ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:victim

# SETUP: a visible blow at the freshly summoned, flat-footed bear. Not counted.
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@while "Take opportunity" y
@while "Die?" n
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:setup

# CONTROL (case B): a visible blow at a bear that is no longer flat-footed.
# The probe's attack line for this one must read flatfoot=0 and sneak=0.
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@while "Take opportunity" y
@while "Die?" n
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:control

# Cast Improved Invisibility on the rogue.
m
@cursorto:mark "Improved Invisibility" DOWN
ENTER
*
@while "Take opportunity" y
@while "Die?" n
@dump:cast

# CASE A: the first blow after the cast. This is the measured blow. Its "pre"
# line must read invisVal=1; then either "hears-you" (surprise lost to Listen)
# or an attack line with sneak=1 (surprise held).
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@while "Take opportunity" y
@while "Die?" n
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:invis-strike

@quit
